WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.878
We are back with another episode
of the Wine Down.

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:06.548
And today we're joined
by the lovely Christina Elmore,

00:00:06.631 --> 00:00:07.716
who plays Condola.

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:10.468
And we'll be discussing
"Lowkey Thankful."

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.762
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.100
Why do you think Condola doesn't
initially invite Lawrence

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.017
to Thanksgiving?

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:20.061
I think that's such
a complicated question.

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:21.938
But I do think, ultimately,

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.274
she's being honest
when she says to him,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.567
"I didn't want to feel pressured

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.861
and I didn't want you
to feel pressure."

00:00:27.944 --> 00:00:29.362
-Mm-hmm.
-I think that we haven't

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:31.990
really gotten to the point yet
where we're talking about like,

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:34.659
meeting families or meeting
even close friends.

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:36.202
-Right.
-And... I just don't feel

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:37.954
-like we're there yet.
-Right.

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:39.873
What was Condola's
thought process?

00:00:39.956 --> 00:00:42.959
Did he sort of invite himself
and now Condola feels put upon?

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.586
-Yeah.
-PRENTICE PENNY:
What's her feelings

00:00:44.669 --> 00:00:45.962
about exposing herself too?

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.882
I think when-- I just went
with the Christina perspective,

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:51.593
which is that like,
I would be really mortified

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:56.181
to say, "Hey! Come to my
very special Friendsgiving

00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:58.558
with all my very best friends."
And then him be like,

00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:00.852
"No, I'm just gonna go get
this Hennessy turkey," like--

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:02.479
-Yeah.
-And so, I think,

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.731
he never brings it up,
I never bring it--

00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:06.274
Because I think we're both
kind of,

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:08.693
afraid of like being vulnerable
in that way.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:12.781
Do you guys feel like Lawrence
is more into the relationship

00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:14.032
than Condola is?

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:18.119
I'm inclined to say no.
I feel like him saying,

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:19.704
"Oh, I didn't know
you wanted a family," and,

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:21.498
"Oh, I'm ready for this
next step,"

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.917
it's more because he's ready
for next steps in his life,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.376
rather than like,
is he actually ready

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.754
for a next step with Condola
at this moment?

00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:28.671
That's fair.

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:32.383
So, do you think that when
she saw Lawrence and Issa

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:33.885
-at the-- the coffee shop--
-Yeah.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:36.763
That they're at your spot,
you feel like Condola left that

00:01:36.846 --> 00:01:39.057
like feeling secure
in her relationship?

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.935
Or do you feel like she left
like, "Oh, there might be

00:01:42.018 --> 00:01:43.353
something I have
to worry about here"?

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.271
I think it was like one
of the first, like,

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:46.981
chinks in the armor.
It was like,

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:50.235
"Oh, Issa and Lawrence
still have jokes that are funny,

00:01:50.318 --> 00:01:53.530
-and that Condola does not get."
-(LAUGHS) That's what hurts.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.739
-It's like...
-That hurts.

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:56.866
"...Y'all are really laughing,
this is not fake pleasantries."

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.661
-It's like--
-It's just like, "Oh, yo--"

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:02.372
And like there's wit
and stuff going back and forth.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:07.544
Do you guys think it's possible
to be friends with your ex

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:10.213
and not have any feelings
for them?

00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:12.549
It's possible,
it's not probable.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.758
(LAUGHING)

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:16.010
-I mean...
-I think it's possible.

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:19.180
I think it's possible.
I just don't see the need to,

00:02:19.264 --> 00:02:20.181
-I guess.
-I don't see the--

00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:21.891
Like, you can have no feelings
for them anymore, sure,

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.811
I think that's totally possible.
But if I don't want

00:02:24.894 --> 00:02:26.479
-to be with you in that way--
-Yeah.

00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:28.273
And I don't have any feelings
for you...

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.358
-Why do we want to be friends?
-Yeah.

00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:33.528
I'm cool with my exes,
but we don't have conversations.

00:02:33.611 --> 00:02:36.197
Like if I saw you in the street
it wouldn't be like, "Die."

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:37.824
It would just be like,
"Oh, hey," joke, joke, joke.

00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:40.034
-Keep it pushing.
-I don't know, I just--

00:02:40.285 --> 00:02:41.161
Well, I don't want to say.

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:42.745
I don't want to see you
do better than me.

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:45.290
-You wouldn't want-- You don't--
-I don't-- No, no.

00:02:45.373 --> 00:02:47.333
I'm the best you got--
ever will have.

00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:48.835
Like, I don't want
to see you out there

00:02:48.918 --> 00:02:49.836
with like a better dude.

00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:51.754
I guess I would never
acknowledge that it was better.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.798
(LAUGHING) I just can't
acknowledge, like--

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:55.300
"Oh, you did that,
that's great."

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:57.010
Yeah, like,
"You got that person--"

00:02:57.093 --> 00:02:58.386
(OVERLAPPING CHATTER)

00:02:58.469 --> 00:02:59.679
"But they're not,
like, better."

00:02:59.762 --> 00:03:00.889
-No.
-No, no.

00:03:00.972 --> 00:03:02.140
And I'm not gonna
acknowledge it.

00:03:02.223 --> 00:03:04.601
-Like he's too tall.
-(CHUCKLES) Yeah.

00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:05.602
Noted.

00:03:05.768 --> 00:03:07.770
Having to stand on tip toes
and stuff.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:10.607
Yeah, he's too--
He's too chiseled, uh-uh.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.275
-That's not real.
-Super secure.

00:03:12.775 --> 00:03:14.694
-Prentice Penny, super...
-I write on Insecure.

00:03:14.777 --> 00:03:16.279
-(CHUCKLES) secure.
-So, there you go.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.072
Hey, thank you again
for joining us.

00:03:18.156 --> 00:03:19.282
See you next time.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:20.867
Cheers!

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.327
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:23.870
Okay.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.788
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

